{"name":"Gratin Dauphinois","hex":"#e0d2a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gratin dauphinois","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A French dish based on potatoes and crème fraîche, from the Dauphiné region"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gratin_dauphinois"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gratin dauphinois","blocks":[{"text":"Gratin dauphinois is a French gratin of sliced raw potatoes baked in cream, from the Dauphiné region in south-eastern France. There are many variants of the name of the dish, including pommes de terre dauphinoise, potatoes à la dauphinoise and gratin de pommes à la dauphinoise."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Gratin_dauphinois.jpg/330px-Gratin_dauphinois.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gratin_dauphinois","wikidata":"Q1647122"},{"title":"Gratin","blocks":[{"text":"Gratin is a culinary technique in which a dish is topped with a browned crust, often using breadcrumbs, cheese, or egg. The term may be applied to any dish made using this method. Gratin is usually prepared in a shallow dish. A gratin is baked or cooked under an overhead grill or broiler to form a golden crust on top, and it is often served in its baking dish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Gratin-Dauphinois.jpg/330px-Gratin-Dauphinois.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gratin","wikidata":"Q1412833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg/500px-8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg/500px-8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=